'''Leia's bedroom'''<ref name="Designing the Galaxy">{{HomeVideoCite|set=Obi-Wan Kenobi: The Complete Series|featurette=Designing the Galaxy}}</ref> was the childhood bedroom of [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] of [[Alderaan]], located on Alderaan in a high tower of the [[Royal Palace of Alderaan|royal palace]] and was considered simple by [[Monarchy|royal]] standards.<ref name="Bloodline" />

==Description==
The room had a [[Viewport|window]] seat with a view of the [[Alderaanian]] [[mountain]] [[Appenza Peak]]<ref name="Leia Princess of Alderaan">''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]''</ref> and a balcony with a chipped [[stone]] from when Organa had gotten carried away with a mock sparring match as a [[Youngling|child]].<ref name="The Princess and the Scoundrel">''[[The Princess and the Scoundrel]]''</ref> The room also had a mantel where the princess kept her [[Leia Organa's keepsake chest|keepsake chest]], that she stored several of her childhood mementos inside including a [[music box]], that played the Alderaanian [[Music|lullaby]] "[[Mirrorbright (song)|Mirrorbright]]," and a baby [[blanket]], made of [[gillendown]].<ref name="Bloodline" />

Organa's bed, an artifact of a grander age, was made from priceless [[Glee Anselm]] [[Wood|hardwoods]] and inlaid with curling lines of pure [[gold]] and [[silver]] with a [[silk]] coverlet. Even though,<ref name="Leia Princess of Alderaan" /> by [[3 BBY]],<ref name="Leia Date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' places [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa's]] birth in [[19 BBY]]. The events of ''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]'' commence just after Organa's sixteenth [[birthday]], which places the events of the novel in [[3 BBY]].</ref> royalty "no longer wasted money on splendor like this", Organa still used the bed as her mother, [[Queen]] [[Breha Organa]], said it was "silly" not to use a "perfectly good bed or [[Crown|tiara]] or palace."<ref name="Leia Princess of Alderaan" />

There was also a vanity table, in the room, with brushes and combs, where Organa's [[Service droid|attendant droid]], [[WA-2V]], would help her get ready, and a cabinet which stored several pieces of jewelry including a pair of silver cuff [[bracelet]]s and a silver [[Leia Organa's silver headband|headband]] with a [[pearl]] charm Organa wore for her [[Leia Organa's Day of Demand|Day of Demand]].<ref name="Leia Princess of Alderaan" />

Organa also kept a [[Wookiee]] [[doll]] in her room which had been gifted to her by her father, [[Viceroy]] [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]]. Bail had given her [[Leia Organa's doll|the doll]] after Organa had met a [[Unidentified Wookiee (Leia Organa)|Wookiee]] for the first time at a state dinner. Organa came to view the doll as a guardian watching over her in her room.<ref name="HS 2">[[Hyperspace Stories 2|''Hyperspace Stories'' 2]]</ref>

==History==
Shortly before her sixteen birthday, Organa's mother visited her in her room and placed the [[Rhindon Sword]] on her bed. The two then had an in depth discussion about love and duty, with her mother explaining the significance of the Rhindon Sword to them and their people, as well as telling Organa that, while she had many duties and obligations to uphold that she still had the freedom to choose and would one day get to choose her own spouse.<ref name="The Princess and the Scoundrel" />

In 3 BBY,<ref name="Leia Date" /> Organa sat at the vanity table in her bedroom where WA-2V helped Organa get ready for her [[Day of Demand]]. After the ceremony was over, Organa returned to her room where she watched a thunderstorm from her window seat, she moved to her bed when WA-2V threatened to forcibly remove her, believing that Organa was in danger. After WA-2V had left, Organa returned to the window seat and opened the window, admiring the storm and looking out at Appenza Peak.<ref name="Leia Princess of Alderaan" />

After learning of her parents involvement in the growing [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|rebellion]], Organa attempted to sleep in her room but found it difficult to fall sleep. Similarly, after Organa had returned from the [[moon]] [[Onoma]], she attempted to fall asleep but found herself thinking about the [[Strike on Onoam|assassination of Quarsh Panaka]], which had just taken place, and the extremist actions of [[Saw Gerrera]] and his [[Partisans]], who had killed him.<ref name="Leia Princess of Alderaan" />

A short while later, Organa was sitting at her vanity, while WA-2V was doing her [[hair]] to greet the guests for her parents dinner party, and realized that the dinner parties, that her parents had recently been excessively throwing, were in fact strategy sessions for their growing rebellion against the [[Galactic Empire]]. After having secretly watched her parents meeting, Organa returned to her room to brush her hair on the window seat, and think over what she'd seen, when her mother, Breha Organa, came in to talk with her. During the conversation, Breha commented that it did do a girl good to fall for a [[Scoundrel/Legends|scoundrel]] every now and then.<ref name="Leia Princess of Alderaan" />

A few [[Standard month|months]] later, WA-2V also helped dress Organa for her [[Coronation of the Alderaanian heir|investment ceremony]] to become [[Crown]] Princess of Alderaan. The night before, Organa had given her [[Keepsake chest]] to her farther, Bail Organa, to show that she had outgrown her use for it,<ref name="Leia Princess of Alderaan" /> with Bail handing it over to his distant cousin, [[Lord]] [[Mellowyn]] of [[Birren]] who kept it at the [[Great Hall of Birren]].<ref name="Bloodline" />

In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Date /> Organa's room in the palace, along with the rest of Alderaan, was [[Destruction of Alderaan|destroyed]] by the Imperial battle station, the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]], under the orders of [[Grand Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]], while Organa was forced to watch as she was held back by [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], who had grabbed Organa by the shoulder.<ref name="A New Hope">{{Film|IV}}</ref>

===Legacy===
As Organa was being escorted back to her cell, after being forced to watch Alderaan's destruction, her room was amongst the things she thought of that were now gone. Thinking that she would do anything to bring them back including trading herself.<ref name="PSFB">''[[A New Hope: The Princess, the Scoundrel, and the Farm Boy]]''</ref>

When Organa was at the shop [[Lost and Found]], on the [[planet]] [[Banas]], with [[Luke Skywalker]],<ref name="HS 2" /> between [[1 ABY]] and [[3 ABY]],<ref name="Hyperspace Date">''Hyperspace Stories'' 2 takes place after [[Luke Skywalker]] is promoted to [[commander]]. [[Star Wars (2015) 55|''Star Wars'' (2015) 55]] establishes that Skywalker was promoted to commander after the [[Battle of Mako-Ta]]. ''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]'' states that the Assault on the [[Mako-Ta Space Docks]] took place twenty [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Proclamation of the New Order|formation]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[19 BBY]]. Therefore, the assault must have taken place in [[1 ABY]]. ''Hyperspace Stories'' 2 alo takes place before [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''The Empire Strikes Back'']], which ''Star Wars: Galactic Atlas'' dates to [[3 ABY]].</ref> she saw a Wookiee doll that reminded her of the one she used to keep in her room. While she and Skywalker were attempting to escape Banas, Organa told Skywalker the story behind the doll.<ref name="HS 2" />

In [[4 ABY]],<ref name="PS Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[The Princess and the Scoundrel]]'' to [[4 ABY]].</ref> shortly after becoming [[Marriage|engaged]] to [[Han Solo]], Organa thought of the small things she lost due to the destruction of Alderaan, amongst other things, she thought about her balcony with the chipped stone and the [[sweetmallow]] [[cake]]s that used to be sent to her room in appeasement when she was too young to attend her parents formal functions.<ref name="The Princess and the Scoundrel" />

==Behind the scenes==
Leia's bedroom first appeared in ''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]'', a [[2017]] young-adult novel written by [[Claudia Gray]].<ref name="Leia Princess of Alderaan" />

